188	  "theorem_statement": "Let g=6 and let B^{bal} be any base carrying a smooth family of genus-6 curves with a balanced tetragonal Casnati\u2013Ekedahl structure (relations bundle F\u2245O_{P^1}(4)\u2295O_{P^1}(5)), universal curve \u03c0:C\u2192B^{bal}, and CE line bundles W_f:=(O_{P(E^\u2228)}(2)\u2297\u03b3^*O_{P^1}(-f))|_C for f\u2208{4,5} (packet convention: W_5 is the f_2=5 summand of (O(2)\u2297\u03b3^*F^\u2228)|_C, not the O_{P^1}(5) summand of F). Write L:=W_5\u2297\u03c9_{C/B}^{-1}. Let Conf_6(C/B^{bal}) be the relative stack of six ordered pairwise-distinct sections, with associated relative divisor \u0393, and let Z^{geo}\u2282Conf_6 be the geometric evaluation-failure locus consisting of geometric points at which the CE obstruction space H^0(C,\u03c9_C\u2297W^\u2228(\u0393)) is nonzero. Then: (A) for every geometric fibre and every effective degree-six divisor \u0393 one has deg(\u03c9_C\u2297W_4^\u2228(\u0393))=\u22124, hence H^0(C,\u03c9_C\u2297W_4^\u2228(\u0393))=0; (B) for every such \u0393 one has deg(\u03c9_C\u2297W_5^\u2228(\u0393))=0, and H^0(C,\u03c9_C\u2297W_5^\u2228(\u0393))\u22600 if and only if O_C(\u0393)\u2245L; (C) consequently Z^{geo} coincides set-theoretically with the Abel\u2013Jacobi incidence locus I^{geo} of geometric points satisfying O_C(\u0393)\u2245L; (D) the locus of reduced-support degree-six effective divisors in the relative effective-divisor space is open (not closed), and the forgetful map from Conf_6 to that reduced-support open is a finite \u00e9tale S_6-torsor on the stack of pairwise-distinct sections, so the ordered reduced failure locus is the preimage of the reduced-support open of the residual incidence for L; (E) on every smooth geometric fibre, \u03c7(L)=1, hence h^0(L)\u22651, so the residual linear system |L| is nonempty and the unordered residual incidence is fibrewise nonempty. This identifies the geometric evaluation-failure locus for the balanced tetragonal CE geometry of packet C66-001-v3; it does not